# title: Down-and-in put
# category: Barriers and touch options
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: An at-the-money put that only comes to life if the stock closes at or below 70% of its initial level at some point.
#
# Knock-in barrier: 70% of the strike-date level, daily closes.
# The building block of every barrier reverse convertible.

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot()
    ki = 0

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() <= 0.70 * s0 then ki = 1 endIf

2028-01-04
    if spot() <= 0.70 * s0 then ki = 1 endIf
    if ki = 1 then pays max(s0 - spot(), 0) endIf
